> Potions of Gain Level seem very infrequent 

Potions of gain level are found almost exclusively
in monster inventory.  You get them by killing the
monsters (usually by killing them in one turn).  
They're not as common as potions of healing, extra
healing, full healing, or object detection; but
you should be getting a few.  If the RNG is in a
good mood, you can end up with a couple dozen of
them by the time you get Gehennom cleaned out.
Even if the RNG is stingy with gain level, though,
you should at least enough be able to find enough to
get yourself up to XL 14 (so you can do the quest)
or 15 (some roles get a useful intrinsic at XL15)
and still perform alchemy, plus a couple of cursed
ones that you will want to keep as escape items.  
If you aren't even getting that many, there are 
several possible explanations:

1. You aren't doing enough damage to kill monsters
   in a single hit very often, especially the kinds
   of monsters that can be generated with a potion
   of gain level.  This is the most likely explanation.
   If you always need multiple turns to kill most
   monsters, you should concentrate on that issue.

2. You are not stealthy, are fumbling, have a habit
   of blowing trumpets or playing drums all the time,
   have the aggravate monster intrinsic (e.g., from
   eating cats, dogs, or your own race), or in some 
   other way are routinely alerting monsters to your 
   presence before you can reach and attack them.

3. The method you are using to kill monsters also
   has the side effect of destroying their potions.

4. You are playing with pacifist conduct or some
   other form of abnormal behavior that is actively
   detrimental to your chances of success.

5. The RNG is being really extremely abnormally
   contrary.  This is the least likely of the five
   explanations I've listed, but it's not entirely
   impossible, in theory.

